fix:
Use an async-aware mutex, or limit the block scope of the standard lock guard so it is dropped before the `.await` point.
```rust
async fn process(data: &Arc<Mutex<State>>) {
    {
        let mut guard = data.lock().unwrap();
        guard.update();
    } // dropped here
    do_something_async().await;
}
```
